summary: the two 95 ms samples were the first request of each round, after a minute of idle. In the control round above (unknown name first) the first request was the slow one (67.6 ms against about 55 ms), so this is a first-request-after-idle effect, not a difference between real and unknown users. Medians over both rounds: existing 56.5 ms, unknown 56.0 ms (1.01x). In the control round "rishi" reached its 5th failure inside 15 minutes and was locked (HTTP 423 in about 2.5 ms), as designed.
